#: assets_dev/worlds/xeen/data_tables/continent_settings.txt:3
msgid "Cloudside"
msgstr ""

#: assets_dev/worlds/xeen/data_tables/continent_settings.txt:4
msgid "Darkside"
msgstr ""

#: assets_dev/worlds/xeen/data_tables/english/autonote.txt:10
msgid ""
"Energy disks (Ellinger needs 20): the Gremlin Court (3), Sharla's sprites and the Temple of Bark (2 and 2), Graalg's ogres (2), the Southern, Western and Eastern Towers (2 each), the Chalice of Protection (2), Gurodel's giants (2), Castle Kalindra's own safes."
msgstr ""

#: assets_dev/worlds/xeen/data_tables/english/autonote.txt:11
msgid ""
"Crodo: the word of the sword vault under Newcastle (M23) is 'laboratory'."
msgstr ""

#: assets_dev/worlds/xeen/data_tables/english/autonote.txt:12
msgid ""
"Artemus's Excavation Permit: Emerson, at Castle Burlock, digs out Newcastle's dungeon for the permit and 5 King's Megacredits."
msgstr ""

#: assets_dev/worlds/xeen/data_tables/english/autonote.txt:13
msgid ""
"The Xeen Slayer Sword: the only blade that can harm Lord Xeen. His castle is in the Clouds of Xeen, above Darzog's tower."
msgstr ""

#: assets_dev/worlds/xeen/data_tables/english/autonote.txt:14
msgid ""
"Dimitri: the disk safes on Castle Kalindra's second floor open to 64-52-31. Ambrose, the Queen's Knight, waits at Griffin Pass."
msgstr ""

#: assets_dev/worlds/xeen/data_tables/english/autonote.txt:15
msgid ""
"Ambrose, the Queen's Knight, flies to Castle Blackfang from Griffin Pass (the Forbidden Zone's south edge). Castle Blackfang has no other way in."
msgstr ""

#: assets_dev/worlds/xeen/data_tables/english/autonote.txt:16
msgid ""
"Queen Kalindra: her bedroom safe on Castle Kalindra's third floor opens to 3-31-62. The crown in it cures her."
msgstr ""

#: assets_dev/worlds/xeen/data_tables/english/autonote.txt:17
msgid ""
"The Great Pyramid, in the Desert of Doom: the Queen's key opens it. The Dragon Pharaoh is on the top floor."
msgstr ""

#: assets_dev/worlds/xeen/data_tables/english/autonote.txt:18
msgid ""
"Corak, in Escape Pod 1 (the Forbidden Zone): he hunted Sheltem across the stars. Sheltem can sense him; he needs a place to hide."
msgstr ""

#: assets_dev/worlds/xeen/data_tables/english/autonote.txt:19
msgid ""
"Olympus, the city of the gods: Lucio's celestial boats from Castleview, Sandcaster and Lakeside, twice a week. The only Soul Box is in Soul Storage."
msgstr ""

#: assets_dev/worlds/xeen/data_tables/english/autonote.txt:20
msgid ""
"Soul Storage, Olympus: the last Soul Box is yours. Corak waits in Escape Pod 1, in the Forbidden Zone."
msgstr ""

#: assets_dev/worlds/xeen/data_tables/english/autonote.txt:21
msgid ""
"A plaque in Soul Storage: all beings have a true name. Alamar's is Sheltem."
msgstr ""

#: assets_dev/worlds/xeen/data_tables/english/autonote.txt:22
msgid ""
"Corak, in the Soul Box: once in Sheltem's presence, throw the box to the ground. Lose the box, or die, and Xeen is doomed."
msgstr ""

#: assets_dev/worlds/xeen/data_tables/english/autonote.txt:23
msgid ""
"Castle Alamar's true-name gate: the four sundials, Fire, Air, Earth and Water Time, must all read nine (Alamar's birth number, says Atlas in Olympus) and the gate asks for Alamar's true name, Sheltem."
msgstr ""

#: assets_dev/worlds/xeen/data_tables/english/autonote.txt:24
msgid ""
"Slick's carnival, before Castle Xeen: Might (100 gold), Speed (1,000 gold), Endurance (5 gems), Accuracy (10 gems). The member who plays needs about 60 in the game's statistic; Slick keeps a free round of tonic under the shooting line. Four dolls buy the Lord Xeen doll."
msgstr ""

#: assets_dev/worlds/xeen/data_tables/english/autonote.txt:25
msgid ""
"The Pharaoh's checklist: the four Reflectors at Cloudside's corners; the four Sleepers on the elemental planes; Prince Roland in the bottom of Sheltem's dungeon; the cloud above Darkstone Tower; the Cube and the Scepter at his shrine."
msgstr ""

#: assets_dev/worlds/xeen/data_tables/english/autonote.txt:26
msgid ""
"The Skyroads' corners: say Fire at the north-west corner, Air at the north-east, Earth at the south-east, Water at the south-west, then step off."
msgstr ""

#: assets_dev/worlds/xeen/data_tables/english/autonote.txt:27
msgid ""
"The Southern Sphinx, in the Desert of the Sphinx: Prince Roland's amulet opens it. The key to the cloud above Darkstone Tower is inside."
msgstr ""

#: assets_dev/worlds/xeen/data_tables/english/autonote.txt:28
msgid ""
"Darkstone Tower, the four heads of the top floor, read down: TYPE \"COMPUTER\" ON LEVEL 4 OF THE DUNGEON OF DEATH. SEE YA SOON!"
msgstr ""

#: assets_dev/worlds/xeen/data_tables/english/autonote.txt:29
msgid ""
"Winterkill: destroy all ghosts, bang the southern gong, re-visit Mayor Randon. Repeat as necessary."
msgstr ""

#: assets_dev/worlds/xeen/data_tables/english/autonote.txt:3
msgid ""
"Crodo's bottle: \"Help! I'm in Darzog's tower!\" Darzog's tower stands on the island in Lake Darzog, west of Rivercity."
msgstr ""

#: assets_dev/worlds/xeen/data_tables/english/autonote.txt:30
msgid ""
"Arie's master's note: the password of Castle Basenji's second-floor door is 'There wolf'. The scroll is on the third floor."
msgstr ""

#: assets_dev/worlds/xeen/data_tables/english/autonote.txt:31
msgid ""
"Jethro's real map: Slibo's cache, on Lakeside's eastern shore, under the cairn of five stones, two paces north. Slibo the wizard camps on Magic Mountain."
msgstr ""

#: assets_dev/worlds/xeen/data_tables/english/autonote.txt:32
msgid ""
"The Dragon Tax Office, at the Dragon Cave's mouth on Mount Firestone: 2,000 gold and 20 gems to see the Dragon King. Dragons who have read Dragon Lore become Great Wyrms there."
msgstr ""

#: assets_dev/worlds/xeen/data_tables/english/autonote.txt:33
msgid ""
"Shangri-La: the hidden valley beyond the Volcano Cave, on Mount Firestone. Its people know a great deal, and teach the rest."
msgstr ""

#: assets_dev/worlds/xeen/data_tables/english/autonote.txt:34
msgid ""
"The Gremlin Court: the burrow under Castleview's wall, outside the north gate. King Gettlewaithe talks big and fights small: beat his guards and he may listen."
msgstr ""

#: assets_dev/worlds/xeen/data_tables/english/autonote.txt:35
msgid ""
"The gremlins are done with Castleview. The gate will open for you now; Mayor Snarfblad owes you."
msgstr ""

#: assets_dev/worlds/xeen/data_tables/english/autonote.txt:36
msgid ""
"Jasper: Castleview Jail. Joe says Jasper stole his map. A map of Joe's would prove what Joe is; the jail's back window is old, too."
msgstr ""

#: assets_dev/worlds/xeen/data_tables/english/autonote.txt:37
msgid ""
"Drawkcab lessons, in order: Brother Otto, Sister Hannah, Brother Bob, Sister Ada (their cells in Castleview)."
msgstr ""

#: assets_dev/worlds/xeen/data_tables/english/autonote.txt:38
msgid ""
"Brother Reger's cell, outside Castleview's walls: say the word the monks study at his door."
msgstr ""

#: assets_dev/worlds/xeen/data_tables/english/autonote.txt:39
msgid ""
"Public Storage: close the numbered chests from 1 to 9, and the lettered ones so they spell PITCHFORK."
msgstr ""

#: assets_dev/worlds/xeen/data_tables/english/autonote.txt:4
msgid ""
"Joe's invoice: Breeder Slimes, 1 mated pair, 287 gold. 5 Doom Bugs at 145 each, 725 gold. Total: 1012 gold. Mayor Gunther will want to see it."
msgstr ""

#: assets_dev/worlds/xeen/data_tables/english/autonote.txt:40
msgid ""
"Rooka, the Queen Rat, nests in the Castleview Sewer. Valio, in the bed, will give you something for her."
msgstr ""

#: assets_dev/worlds/xeen/data_tables/english/autonote.txt:41
msgid ""
"The Western Tower's key is on its top floor. The heretics haul their supplies up a rope on the tower's north wall."
msgstr ""

#: assets_dev/worlds/xeen/data_tables/english/autonote.txt:42
msgid ""
"The Western Tower's ground door is open. Dreyfus waits for news in the Temple of Mok."
msgstr ""

#: assets_dev/worlds/xeen/data_tables/english/autonote.txt:43
msgid ""
"Gemsmiths: Linus (ruby, 2 gems), Simon (emerald, 4), Toby (sapphire, 6), Hector (diamond, 10), each for five rocks. Rocks: the Gemstone Mines; diamonds only from the north adit, in the Forbidden Zone."
msgstr ""

#: assets_dev/worlds/xeen/data_tables/english/autonote.txt:44
msgid ""
"Vespar's emerald handle: somewhere on the road from Sandcaster, east of the Sprite Forest. Sandcaster admits only pass holders."
msgstr ""

#: assets_dev/worlds/xeen/data_tables/english/autonote.txt:45
msgid ""
"Monga melons: the southern meadows of Castleview Vale, among the centipedes. Nibbler wants three."
msgstr ""

#: assets_dev/worlds/xeen/data_tables/english/autonote.txt:46
msgid ""
"Princess Sheewana is held by Shaalth's Orcs in the Temple of Bark, the great tree in Sprite Forest. Nibbler has the key."
msgstr ""

#: assets_dev/worlds/xeen/data_tables/english/autonote.txt:47
msgid "Sheewana is free and on her way home to Sharla's treehouse."
msgstr ""

#: assets_dev/worlds/xeen/data_tables/english/autonote.txt:48
msgid ""
"Ogre Pass, in Sprite Forest: Graalg's Ogres and their two forts. Kramer pays to be rid of them, a bounty if both forts burn."
msgstr ""

#: assets_dev/worlds/xeen/data_tables/english/autonote.txt:49
msgid ""
"Thieves' Guild letter: the Trolls have stolen the guild's gold. The troll holes of Sprite Forest lead down to Hobstadt, the Troll King."
msgstr ""

#: assets_dev/worlds/xeen/data_tables/english/autonote.txt:5
msgid ""
"Artemus: Baron Darzog, the King's master sorcerer, was jealous of Crodo. Both vanished. Darzog's tower stands on the island in Lake Darzog."
msgstr ""

#: assets_dev/worlds/xeen/data_tables/english/autonote.txt:50
msgid ""
"Xenoc the Wizard and Morgana the Sorceress rule Sandcaster's guilds from the wizard quarter. They cannot be talked down: defeat them, then see Astra."
msgstr ""

#: assets_dev/worlds/xeen/data_tables/english/autonote.txt:51
msgid ""
"Xenoc and Morgana are dead. The wizard quarter of Sandcaster is open: the Guild of Night, Esoterica and the three towers."
msgstr ""

#: assets_dev/worlds/xeen/data_tables/english/autonote.txt:52
msgid ""
"The gargoyles roost on Magic Mountain, above Lakeside. Caleb's glass is probably in their lair."
msgstr ""

#: assets_dev/worlds/xeen/data_tables/english/autonote.txt:53
msgid ""
"The Northern Tower, in the Desert of Doom: the Voweless Knights. On the top floor a voice asks what you seek: answer without vowels, Chlc."
msgstr ""

#: assets_dev/worlds/xeen/data_tables/english/autonote.txt:54
msgid ""
"The Voweless Knights' answers (Librarian Ormond's copy): Let sleeping dogs lie. He who laughs last, laughs best. The needs of the many outweigh the needs of the few. Love of money is the root of all evil. Don't look a gift horse in the mouth. A fool and his money are soon parted. If wishes were horses, beggars would ride. And what their voice wants to hear you seek: Chlc."
msgstr ""

#: assets_dev/worlds/xeen/data_tables/english/autonote.txt:55
msgid ""
"The Jewel of Ages is in the Great Eastern Tower, east of Sandcaster, with the mages who bought it. The key was in the thieves' Ali Baba chest."
msgstr ""

#: assets_dev/worlds/xeen/data_tables/english/autonote.txt:56
msgid ""
"Ellinger's sealed letter, for the Guildmaster of Sandcaster: Nasir, of the Guild of Light."
msgstr ""

#: assets_dev/worlds/xeen/data_tables/english/autonote.txt:57
msgid ""
"The thieves' ledger: the Jewel of Ages and the Griffin statuette sold to the mages of the Eastern Tower, east of Sandcaster; the Dragon to the Head Witch of Lakeside; the Pegasus to the head heretical cleric of the Western Tower."
msgstr ""

#: assets_dev/worlds/xeen/data_tables/english/autonote.txt:58
msgid ""
"Luna's statuettes: start with the thieves of the Great Southern Tower. The fountain keeper near Venom Pond has its key."
msgstr ""

#: assets_dev/worlds/xeen/data_tables/english/autonote.txt:59
msgid ""
"Lakeside's coven: the Guild's door asks 'What am I?' (the answer is witch). Four prisoners in the cells below, the Head Witch above them; Naomi in the stocks on the square."
msgstr ""

#: assets_dev/worlds/xeen/data_tables/english/autonote.txt:6
msgid "Newcastle: walls built (5 Megacredits). Next, a keep: 5 more."
msgstr ""

#: assets_dev/worlds/xeen/data_tables/english/autonote.txt:60
msgid ""
"The Head Witch keeps her pass to Necropolis in a chest in her room, in the coven's north-west corner."
msgstr ""

#: assets_dev/worlds/xeen/data_tables/english/autonote.txt:61
msgid ""
"Sandro's heart is in a jar in the Necropolis Sewer. Bring it to him, and he can die."
msgstr ""

#: assets_dev/worlds/xeen/data_tables/english/autonote.txt:62
msgid ""
"The Enchanted Boulders of the Desert of Doom keep a dead paladin's armour. One of them asks: What am I?"
msgstr ""

#: assets_dev/worlds/xeen/data_tables/english/autonote.txt:63
msgid ""
"The tribble note, in four pieces from the drains of the Olympus sewer: TR, IB, BL, ES."
msgstr ""

#: assets_dev/worlds/xeen/data_tables/english/autonote.txt:64
msgid "Obelisk in Vertigo Meadows: the first of seven Cloudside words, SEEK."
msgstr ""

#: assets_dev/worlds/xeen/data_tables/english/autonote.txt:65
msgid "Obelisk by Rivercity: the second Cloudside word, THE."
msgstr ""

#: assets_dev/worlds/xeen/data_tables/english/autonote.txt:66
msgid "Obelisk in Lifeforce Lagoon: the third Cloudside word, HOARD."
msgstr ""

#: assets_dev/worlds/xeen/data_tables/english/autonote.txt:67
msgid "Obelisk in Burlock Savannah: the fourth Cloudside word, BURIED."
msgstr ""

#: assets_dev/worlds/xeen/data_tables/english/autonote.txt:68
msgid "Obelisk in Winterkill Tundra: the fifth Cloudside word, FOR."
msgstr ""

#: assets_dev/worlds/xeen/data_tables/english/autonote.txt:69
msgid "Obelisk in the Desert of the Sphinx: the sixth Cloudside word, THE."
msgstr ""

#: assets_dev/worlds/xeen/data_tables/english/autonote.txt:7
msgid ""
"Megacredits: the Temple of Yak (Rivercity's south woods), the Tomb of a Thousand Terrors (Lifeforce Lagoon), the Golem Dungeon (Winterkill Tundra, by the lagoon)."
msgstr ""

#: assets_dev/worlds/xeen/data_tables/english/autonote.txt:70
msgid "Obelisk on Mount Firestone: the seventh Cloudside word, SPHINX."
msgstr ""

#: assets_dev/worlds/xeen/data_tables/english/autonote.txt:71
msgid "Obelisk in Castleview Vale: the first of six Darkside words, DIG."
msgstr ""

#: assets_dev/worlds/xeen/data_tables/english/autonote.txt:72
msgid "Obelisk in the Sprite Forest: the second Darkside word, BENEATH."
msgstr ""

#: assets_dev/worlds/xeen/data_tables/english/autonote.txt:73
msgid "Obelisk by Sandcaster: the third Darkside word, THE."
msgstr ""

#: assets_dev/worlds/xeen/data_tables/english/autonote.txt:74
msgid "Obelisk by Lakeside: the fourth Darkside word, BROKEN."
msgstr ""

#: assets_dev/worlds/xeen/data_tables/english/autonote.txt:75
msgid "Obelisk in the Desert of Doom: the fifth Darkside word, TRAVEL."
msgstr ""

#: assets_dev/worlds/xeen/data_tables/english/autonote.txt:76
msgid "Obelisk in the Forbidden Zone: the sixth Darkside word, PYRAMID."
msgstr ""

#: assets_dev/worlds/xeen/data_tables/english/autonote.txt:8
msgid ""
"Newcastle: keep built (5 Megacredits). A smith and a training hall work there now."
msgstr ""

#: assets_dev/worlds/xeen/data_tables/english/autonote.txt:9
msgid ""
"Madame Oorla: the Dragon Pharaoh's orb must go to Ellinger first. His tower's word is his own name."
msgstr ""

#: assets_dev/worlds/xeen/data_tables/english/award_texts.txt:3
msgid "Won %u Page battles in the Warzone."
msgstr ""

#: assets_dev/worlds/xeen/data_tables/english/award_texts.txt:4
msgid "Won %u Squire battles in the Warzone."
msgstr ""

#: assets_dev/worlds/xeen/data_tables/english/award_texts.txt:5
